  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">FemFocus - Women, Peace and Security - Stichting Cordaid-  West-Africa - Mali &amp; Niger</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The programme will be implemented in Mali and Niger and contributes to the Women, Peace and Security (sub)objectives of FemFocus. Both countries face entrenched insecurity due to armed conflict and violent extremism, political and economic fragility, weakened public service provision, food insecurity and climate-induced shocks and displacement. Recent military coups, shifts in security partnerships, exit from ECOWAS and a reduction in development aid have further constrained civic space and undermined progress on gender equality, increasing risks of SGBV (including CRSV) and limiting women&#x2019;s mobility, livelihoods and access to protection, legal and psychosocial services.

The programme addresses fragility, insecurity and conflict by strengthening women&#x2019;s participation and leadership in peace, human security and governance processes. It delivers funding, capacity strengthening, and protection for women-led organisations, building institutional resilience. 

Cordaid will finance and strengthen in-country partners in Mali en Niger. Financing and capacity strengthening activities will promote:

&#x2022; Women&#x2019;s leadership in conflict prevention and mediation through training, mentorship, networking among women mediators, and community dialogue with religious leaders and authorities.

&#x2022; Meaningful participation of women in peace and security through accessible activities that expand women&#x2019;s public, political, and civic engagement. Cross-border exchanges support learning on NAP-1325 implementation, strengthen coordinated WPS advocacy and advance Local Action Plans (LAPs).

&#x2022; Supporting survivors of CRSV by improving access to survivor-centered services, including medical care, MHPSS, legal aid, safe referrals, and (economic) recovery. It strengthens (in)formal justice and community actors through early warning and survivor-centred approaches. The prevention of SGBV is key and addressed by strengthening women&#x2019;s voice in security processes and addressing harmful norms.

Desired results:

- Women&#x2019;s leadership in conflict prevention and mediation in Mali and Niger is strengthened.
- Women&#x2019;s meaningful participation and influence in formal and informal peace and security decision-making spaces is increased.
- Survivors and victims of CRSV and SGBV have improved access to coordinated, quality, survivor-centred services and protection.</narrative>
  </description>
